Sval: a press of play plays the video on a site that asks first

Under media.autoplay.site-permission-only a click or key press on a page
allows nothing, because a page can call play() from any input. On a site
that asks first, a play() made inside the handler of the user's press is
allowed: the test media.autoplay.blocking_policy's user-input-depth policy
makes (UserActivation::IsHandlingUserInput). A player's play button calls
play() there, Gecko's own controls included, and a play() the page makes
later, from a timer or after a load the press started, does not. Always
deny and a tab's DENY refuse the press.

A play() the press allowed sends SvalMediaPressPlayed, chrome-only, which
the Autoplay actor forwards to the tab, so the front end can allow media
for the rest of the visit. With the pref off nothing changes.

diff --git a/dom/media/autoplay/AutoplayPolicy.cpp b/dom/media/autoplay/AutoplayPolicy.cpp
index 8783bad41e..65e7be7297 100644
--- a/dom/media/autoplay/AutoplayPolicy.cpp
+++ b/dom/media/autoplay/AutoplayPolicy.cpp
@@ -145,6 +145,31 @@ static bool IsWindowAllowedToPlayBySitePermission(nsPIDOMWindowInner* aWindow) {
   return IsWindowAllowedToPlayByTraits(aWindow);
 }
 
+// Under media.autoplay.site-permission-only, whether the site's answer is ask
+// first: BLOCKED_ALL, its own or, for a site with none, the default's. Always
+// deny, the site's DENY or the default's, and a tab's DENY for a visit the
+// user stopped, refuse every press.
+static bool SiteAsksFirst(nsPIDOMWindowInner* aWindow) {
+  const uint32_t perm = SiteAutoplayPerm(aWindow);
+  return perm == nsIAutoplay::BLOCKED_ALL ||
+         (perm == nsIPermissionManager::UNKNOWN_ACTION &&
+          StaticPrefs::media_autoplay_site_permission_only_default() == 0);
+}
+
+// On a site that asks first, a media element plays when play() runs inside
+// the handler of the user's press, the test media.autoplay.blocking_policy's
+// user-input-depth policy makes. A player's own play button calls play()
+// there, and a play() the page makes later, from a timer or after a load the
+// press started, does not.
+static bool IsAllowedToPlayByPress(const HTMLMediaElement& aElement) {
+  if (UserActivation::IsHandlingUserInput() &&
+      SiteAsksFirst(aElement.OwnerDoc()->GetInnerWindow())) {
+    AUTOPLAY_LOG("Allow autoplay as play() is called inside user input.");
+    return true;
+  }
+  return false;
+}
+
